  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Cucumis anguria",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cucumis_anguria",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1369817692,
      "text": "Cucumis anguria, commonly known as maroon cucumber, West Indian gherkin, maxixe, burr gherkin, cackrey, and West Indian gourd, is a vine that is indigenous to Africa, but has become naturalized in the New World, and is cultivated in many places. It is similar and related to the common cucumber (C. sativus) and its cultivars are known as gherkins."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Cucumis anguria",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cucumis_anguria",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 167903565,
      "text": "Cucumis anguria, generalmente conocido como pepinillo, pepino del monte, pepino silvestre, pepinillo de las indias occidentales, pepinillo erizo, sandía de la víbora o pepino cimarrón, es una cucurbitácea originaria de África, pero que se ha naturalizado en el Nuevo Mundo, y está cultivado en muchos sitios. Es similar y relacionado al pepino común."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Cucumis anguria",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cucumis_anguria",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 237057901,
      "text": "Cucumis anguria, le concombre des Antilles, « concombre piquant » en Guyane, ti-concombre ou macissis, est une espèce de plantes à fleurs dicotylédones de la famille des Cucurbitaceae, originaire d'Afrique australe."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Maxixe (hortaliça)",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maxixe_(hortali%C3%A7a)",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 73001303,
      "text": "Cucumis anguria, conhecido popularmente como maxixe, é uma planta rasteira ou trepadeira anual e de clima quente. Aos seus frutos comestíveis, também se dá o nome maxixe ou, regionalmente, nalgumas partes do Brasil, galinha-arrepiada."
    }
